    {
      "abstract": "$p_{\\rm {T}}$-integrated prompt $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$ baryon cross section in pp collisions at $\\sqrt{s} = 5.02$ TeV in the rapidity interval $|y|<0.5$, and in p-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm {NN}}} = 5.02$ TeV in the rapidity interval $-0.96 \\lt y \\lt 0.04$.\nFirst column: The $p_{\\rm {T}}$-integrated cross section in the visible (measured) $p_{\\rm {T}}$ region, which in pp collisions is $1 \\lt p_{\\rm T} \\lt 12$ GeV/c and in p-Pb collisions is $1 \\lt p_{\\rm T} \\lt 24$ GeV/c. The second (sys) error is from the luminosity uncertainty.\nSecond column: The $p_{\\rm {T}}$-integrated cross section extrapolated to all $p_{\\rm {T}}$. The second (sys) error is from the luminosity uncertainty and the third (sys) error is from the extrapolation to the full $p_{\\rm {T}}$ range.",
