  "data_abstract": "The production cross section of prompt $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$ charmed baryons was measured with the ALICE detector at the LHC at midrapidity in proton-proton (pp) and proton-lead (p-Pb) collisions at a centre-of-mass energy per nucleon pair of $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm {NN}}} = 5.02$ TeV. The $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$ and $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{-}$ baryons were reconstructed in the hadronic decay channels $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+} \\to {\\rm p} {\\rm K}^{-}\\pi^{+}$ and $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+} \\to {\\rm p} {\\rm K}^{0}_{S}$ and respective charge conjugates. The measured differential cross sections as a function of transverse momentum ($p_{\\rm {T}}$) and the $p_{\\rm {T}}$-integrated $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$ production cross section in pp and in p-Pb collisions are presented. The $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$ nuclear modification factor ($R_\\mathrm{pPb}$), calculated from the cross sections in pp and in p-Pb collisions, is presented and compared with the $R_\\mathrm{pPb}$ of D mesons. The $\\Lambda_{\\rm {c}}^{+}$/${\\rm D}^{0}$ ratio is also presented and compared with the light-flavour baryon-to-meson ratios p$/\\pi$ and $\\Lambda / {\\rm K}^{0}_{S}$, and measurements from other LHC experiments. The results are compared to predictions from model calculations and Monte Carlo event generators.",
